Package: LocusPick
Type: Package
Title: Transparent Selection of Representative Loci for Genome Browser
        Figures
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Garrett", "Evensen", email = "kgsevensen@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Kathryn", "Lande", role = "aut"))
Description: Representative genome browser tracks in papers are usually picked
    by eye. LocusPick replaces that with a reproducible, auditable workflow.
    It links binding peaks (ChIP-seq, CUT&RUN, ATAC-seq) to genes, places genes
    into groups defined by two differential expression contrasts (for example a
    factor knockout and an aging or treatment contrast), runs quality checks
    that catch common pitfalls (peak-to-gene assignments that disagree with the
    gene models, low-mappability paralog regions, gaps in signal coverage,
    outdated gene symbols), ranks candidate loci with explicit weights, and
    draws multi-track locus plots with expression insets. Every candidate and
    every quality flag is written to a table so the choice of examples can be
    reported and reproduced.
